Run a 30-minute inspection of `agent-roguelite`. Always delegate Codex tasks through `~/.claude/bin/codex-sub` using the subscription `gpt-6-luna` model; I will not write the code myself.

1) Use `ps` to check for `codex exec` processes. There are currently three tasks, with logs at `scratchpad/codex-prompts/<name>.log` and `.wrap.log`, and `OUTBOX`/`INBOX` under `scratchpad/box/<directory>/`:
- `eqfix`: leftover issues in the equipment UI; worktree `agent-roguelite-worktrees/ui-equipment-wow`; box `box/eqfix`
- `a0`: A0 command-layer skeleton; worktree `.../commands-a0`; box `box/a0`
- `g1`: Design Graph G1 (JSON is authoritative, one-way graph import, read-only for partners); worktree `.../design-graph-g1`; box `box/g1`

For each task, check the log's last-modified time, new `OUTBOX` entries, `git log main..HEAD`, `git status`, and whether `codex-exit` exists. If the log has not changed for more than 15 minutes while the process is still running, treat it as possibly stuck and inspect the end of the log for the cause. If you see `[GATE]` or `[BLOCKED]`, read the supporting evidence and reply in `INBOX.md`.

2) When a task finishes, read the final report, create a fresh scratchpad copy yourself with both Library and Art, rerun all EditMode tests and `tools/run-bot-watched.sh`, and, for UI tasks, render the UI and open the screenshot for a manual check. Do not trust Codex's claims; verify with your own `git status` and `git diff`.

3) Rules: Leave branches containing functional changes (gameplay, UI, or behavior) for user acceptance; do not merge them. Pure tooling or documentation changes may be merged. If G1 passes acceptance, its data format becomes the prerequisite for R2.

4) Follow-up queue (handle items one at a time, and parallelize only when it is genuinely safe; do not force parallel execution):
- After G1 passes acceptance, delegate R2 (make moves data-driven), based on `feature/refactor-actor`, and merge in G1's data format.
- After both G1 and `eqfix` pass acceptance, delegate a redesign of the talent page to resemble the World of Warcraft talent tree, based on the UI-chain branch.
- After A0 is accepted, report to the user before starting A1.
- R1 cleanup was already committed as `ac9b031`; wait for the user's confirmation.

5) Report "no changes" only when no tasks are running and the queue is empty.
